Package: QRfs
Type: Package
Title: Fixed-Smoothing Uniform Inference for Quantile Regression
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Kaicheng", "Chen", role = "aut"),
    person("Antonio F.", "Galvao", role = "aut"),
    person("Seunghwa", "Rho", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "srhoecon@hanyang.ac.kr"),
    person("Timothy J.", "Vogelsang", role = "aut"),
    person("Jungmo", "Yoon", role = "aut"))
Description: Fixed-b and fixed-K heteroskedasticity and autocorrelation robust (HAR) inference for
    time-series quantile regression, following Chen, Galvao, Rho, Vogelsang and Yoon (2026),
    "Fixed-smoothing Uniform Inference for Quantile Regression": stack-Wald tests of joint
    restrictions at specified quantiles, uniform sup tests over a range of quantiles with uniform
    confidence bands, tests that a coefficient is constant or monotone in the quantile, and the
    conventional small-b or large-K test with chi-square critical values. One kernel (Bartlett)
    and one orthonormal series basis (DCT-II), with test-based and MSE-optimal data-dependent
    smoothing. Includes the growth-vulnerability data of Adrian, Boyarchenko and Giannone (2019)
    <doi:10.1257/aer.20161923>.
License: GPL (>= 3)
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 3.6.0)
Imports: quantreg, Matrix, mvtnorm, stats, graphics, utils
Suggests: pbivnorm
LazyData: true
URL: https://github.com/seunghwaRho/QRfs
